{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nThe task SE-PE-01 is about grammar-guided node reduction (Perses-style syntax-guided reduction). Let me understand what needs to be done:\n\n1. We have a tree of nodes, each with: id, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility\n2. We have required_symbols that must remain represented in the tree\n3. We need to reduce the tree by removing nodes while preserving required symbols\n\nThe rules:\n- Never remove root, a required symbol node, or a node with retained children\n- Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\n- Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes (process deeper first)\n- Use node ID as stable tie-break at equal depth\n- Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order\n\nLet me think about the algorithm:\n\n1. Process nodes from deepest to shallowest (descending depth order)\n2. At equal depth, use node ID as tie-break (ascending alphabetical/lexicographic order)\n3. For each node (in this order):\n   - Skip if not removable\n   - Skip if it's root\n   - Skip if its symbol is in required_symbols\n   - Skip if it has retained children\n   - Try removing it: check if all required symbols still have at least one retained node\n   - If yes, remove it (add to removed list)\n   - Otherwise, keep it\n\nWait, let me re-read: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\"\n\nSo a node can be removed if:\n- It's removable\n- It's not root\n- Its symbol is not a required symbol\n- It has no retained children (all its children have already been removed)\n- Removing it still keeps all required symbols represented\n\nThe order: consider deeper nodes first (higher depth first), and at equal depth, use node ID as stable tie-break (alphabetical order).\n\nLet me trace through case 000:\n\nNodes:\n- root: depth=0, removable=false, symbol=root\n- n1: depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s1\n- n2: depth=1, removable=true, symbol=s2\n- n3: depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s0\n- n4: depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s1, parent=n2\n- n5: depth=2, removable=false, symbol=s2, parent=n3\n- n6: depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s0, parent=n1\n\nrequired_symbols: [root, s1]\n\nSort order (deepest first, then by node ID):\n- depth 2: n4, n5, n6 (alphabetically: n4, n5, n6)\n- depth 1: n1, n2, n3\n- depth 0: root\n\nProcess n4 (depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s1):\n- Symbol s1 is in required_symbols → cannot remove (symbol is required)\n- Keep n4\n\nProcess n5 (depth=2, removable=false, symbol=s2):\n- Not removable → skip\n- Keep n5\n\nProcess n6 (depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s0):\n- Symbol s0 not in required_symbols\n- No retained children (leaf)\n- If removed: remaining symbols would be {root (root), s1 (n1), s2 (n2), s0 (n3), s1 (n4), s2 (n5)}\n  - s1 is still there (n1 has s1), root is still there\n  - All required symbols represented → can remove\n- Remove n6. removed_list = [n6]\n\nProcess n1 (depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s1):\n- Not removable → keep n1\n\nProcess n2 (depth=1, removable=true, symbol=s2):\n- Symbol s2 not in required_symbols\n- Check retained children of n2: n4 is retained (kept because it has required symbol s1)\n- n2 has retained children → cannot remove\n- Keep n2\n\nProcess n3 (depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s0):\n- Not removable → keep n3\n\nProcess root (depth=0, removable=false):\n- Not removable → keep root\n\nResult:\n- removed: [n6]\n- retained: [root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5]\n\nLet me verify the output format:\n- removed_node_ids: [\"n6\"] (in removal order)\n- retained_node_ids: sorted list: [\"n1\", \"n2\", \"n3\", \"n4\", \"n5\", \"root\"]\n\nWait, \"Return sorted retained IDs\" - sorted how? Probably alphabetically/lexicographically.\n\nLet me now think about what \"required symbols remain represented\" means - it means at least one retained node must have that symbol.\n\nNow let me code this up:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Build node lookup\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    \n    # Build children map\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    for n in nodes:\n        if n[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            children[n[\"parent\"]].append(n[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Track retained set\n    retained = {n[\"id\"] for n in nodes}\n    \n    # Sort nodes: deepest first, then by node ID (alphabetical) as tiebreak\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    removed_order = []\n    \n    for node in sorted_nodes:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        \n        # Must be removable\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Never remove root (also covered by removable=false, but be safe)\n        if node[\"symbol\"] == \"root\" or node[\"parent\"] is None:\n            continue\n        \n        # Never remove a required symbol node\n        if node[\"symbol\"] in required_symbols:\n            continue\n        \n        # Never remove a node with retained children\n        has_retained_children = any(c in retained for c in children[nid])\n        if has_retained_children:\n            continue\n        \n        # Tentatively remove: check all required symbols still represented\n        retained.discard(nid)\n        \n        # Check if all required symbols are still in retained nodes\n        retained_symbols = {node_map[rid][\"symbol\"] for rid in retained}\n        \n        if required_symbols.issubset(retained_symbols):\n            # Keep removed\n            removed_order.append(nid)\n        else:\n            # Restore\n            retained.add(nid)\n    \n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removed_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_sorted\n    }\n```\n\nLet me trace through case 001 to verify:\n\nNodes:\n- root: depth=0, removable=false, symbol=root\n- n1: depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s1\n- n2: depth=1, removable=true, symbol=s2\n- n3: depth=1, removable=false, symbol=s0\n- n4: depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s1, parent=n2\n- n5: depth=2, removable=false, symbol=s2, parent=n3\n- n6: depth=2, removable=true, symbol=s0, parent=n1\n\nrequired_symbols: [root, s1]\n\nSame structure as case 000!\n\nProcess n4 (symbol=s1, required) → keep\nProcess n5 (not removable) → keep\nProcess n6 (removable, symbol=s0):\n- No retained children\n- Remove tentatively: retained = {root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5}\n- Symbols: {root, s1, s2, s0, s1, s2} → root and s1 present → remove\n- removed = [n6]\n\nProcess n1 (not removable) → keep\nProcess n2 (removable, symbol=s2):\n- Has retained children: n4 (retained) → cannot remove\nProcess n3 (not removable) → keep\nProcess root (not removable) → keep\n\nSame result as case 000.\n\nCase 002 is the same structure too. All three cases have identical tree structure and required_symbols, just different utility values. The utility values don't affect the algorithm based on the description (the algorithm is purely structural).\n\nThe solution looks correct. Let me finalize the code.\n\nActually wait - I need to re-read: \"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth.\" - The tie break is node ID, and since n4, n5, n6 all start with \"n\" followed by numbers, alphabetical order gives n4 \u003c n5 \u003c n6 which matches numeric order here. That should be fine.\n\nAlso, I'm sorting alphabetically for retained_node_ids. \"root\" comes after \"n\" alphabetically? Let me check: 'r' \u003e 'n' in ASCII, so \"root\" \u003e \"n*\". So sorted would be: n1, n2, n3, n4, n5, n6, ... then root. Wait, n6 is removed in our case, so: n1, n2, n3, n4, n5, root.\n\nActually \"Return sorted retained IDs\" - I'll just use Python's default sort which is lexicographic.\n\nThe implementation looks good. Let me write the final JSON response.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    required_symbols = set(case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"])\\n\\n    # Build lookup and children map\\n    node_map = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: [] for n in nodes}\\n    for n in nodes:\\n        if n[\\\"parent\\\"] is not None:\\n            children[n[\\\"parent\\\"]].append(n[\\\"id\\\"])\\n\\n    # Start with all nodes retained\\n    retained = {n[\\\"id\\\"] for n in nodes}\\n\\n    # Process deepest first; use node ID as stable tiebreak at equal depth\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\\\"depth\\\"], n[\\\"id\\\"]))\\n\\n    removed_order = []\\n\\n    for node in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = node[\\\"id\\\"]\\n\\n        # Must be flagged removable\\n        if not node[\\\"removable\\\"]:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Never remove root (parent is None)\\n        if node[\\\"parent\\\"] is None:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Never remove a node whose symbol is required\\n        if node[\\\"symbol\\\"] in required_symbols:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Never remove a node that still has retained children\\n        if any(c in retained for c in children[nid]):\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Tentatively remove and check interestingness (all required symbols still present)\\n        retained.discard(nid)\\n        retained_symbols = {node_map[rid][\\\"symbol\\\"] for rid in retained}\\n\\n        if required_symbols.issubset(retained_symbols):\\n            # Removal is valid; record it\\n            removed_order.append(nid)\\n        else:\\n            # Restore: removing this node would lose a required symbol\\n            retained.add(nid)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removed_order,\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": sorted(retained)\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_01oG1h4fjsH9eXa4flMF3bU8","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2398},"cache_creation_input_tokens":2398,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":62,"output_tokens":2750,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2255},"service_tier":"standard"}}